From: lain3d <eyeofsteiner@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: Add CameraSensorHelper for Sony IMX681

The IMX681 is the front camera on the Surface Pro 11 (x1e80100), reached
through the qcom-camss simple pipeline handler and the software ISP.

Without a helper, IPASoft cannot convert an analogue gain code into a
gain and logs:

    IPASoft: Failed to create camera sensor helper for imx681

Its AE loop then reasons with the wrong model. On this module it settles
at exposure 3546 (the maximum) and gain code 18, which is 1.02x, while a
dim indoor scene needs a code around 1014 (102x). Frames flow and the
preview is black.

The sensor uses Sony's usual reciprocal gain law, gain = 1024/(1024 - x),
the same constants as IMX477 and IMX708. Determined by measurement rather
than a datasheet: a gain sweep was captured through the qcom-camss RDI
path and `gain = C/(D - code)` solved pairwise over the ten combinations
of codes 900, 960, 1000, 1014 and 1020, using per-frame medians so that a
few per cent of clipped highlights could not skew the fit. That gives
D = 1026 at the measured black level, bracketing the conventional 1024.

Black level is 0x40 at 10 bits, also measured: dark frames sit at 15-16
of 255 on the high byte of each RAW10 pixel, i.e. 62-64 at 10 bits.

Deliberately not adding a camera_sensor_properties entry: that needs the
physical unit cell size, which is not known for this module, and guessing
it would be worse than the current defaulted values.

Signed-off-by: lain3d <eyeofsteiner@gmail.com>
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -642,6 +642,18 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx477", CameraSensorHelperImx477)

+class CameraSensorHelperImx681 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperImx681()
+	{
+		/* Measured on a Surface Pro 11 module: 0x40 at 10 bits. */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 0, 1024, -1, 1024 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx681", CameraSensorHelperImx681)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperImx708 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
